WEBVTT

00:00:05.023 --> 00:00:06.454
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:06.772 --> 00:00:07.658
Sammy!

00:00:08.454 --> 00:00:10.635
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can! Go!

00:00:14.632 --> 00:00:15.655
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:16.359 --> 00:00:17.722
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:21.817 --> 00:00:22.817
This is dad's book.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.617
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:25.162 --> 00:00:26.775
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:26.844 --> 00:00:27.957
Family business.

00:00:28.116 --> 00:00:29.502
Do you think Mom wanted all this for us?

00:00:29.593 --> 00:00:30.706
I can't do this alone.

00:00:31.521 --> 00:00:32.520
I'm driving.

00:01:19.766 --> 00:01:21.379
Can't keep kids out of this place.

00:01:21.629 --> 00:01:22.765
What is it anyway?

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:24.287
I forgot you're not a local.

00:01:24.446 --> 00:01:25.469
You don't know the legend.

00:01:25.878 --> 00:01:26.650
Legend?

00:01:26.832 --> 00:01:28.768
Every town's got its stories, right?

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.836
Ours is Roosevelt asylum.

00:01:31.518 --> 00:01:33.790
They say it's haunted with
the ghosts of the patients.

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:35.113
Spend the night,

00:01:35.613 --> 00:01:37.340
Spirits will drive you insane.

00:01:43.859 --> 00:01:44.791
Hello?!

00:01:45.222 --> 00:01:46.313
Police officers!

00:01:49.448 --> 00:01:50.812
Police officers!

00:01:59.366 --> 00:02:01.974
You tell me these kids
brought bolt cutters?

00:02:03.092 --> 00:02:03.865
Come on.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:05.024
Let's split up.

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:06.523
All right.

00:02:20.724 --> 00:02:21.565
Hello?

00:02:50.516 --> 00:02:51.356
Hello?

00:03:14.964 --> 00:03:15.918
All right.

00:03:16.827 --> 00:03:18.076
Come on out.

00:03:46.491 --> 00:03:47.627
Kelly, you copy?

00:03:49.694 --> 00:03:50.558
Jeez!

00:03:51.376 --> 00:03:52.443
Where the hell you been?!

00:03:52.602 --> 00:03:53.398
In there.

00:03:53.511 --> 00:03:54.647
What was it? See anything?

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:58.677
No.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.639
This is patrol 1 4. We are
clear, we return to the station

00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:28.351
Hey.

00:04:36.541 --> 00:04:37.540
So, what?

00:04:38.381 --> 00:04:39.812
You're still not talking to me?

00:04:43.018 --> 00:04:43.814
Walt.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.927
I said I was sorry about before.

00:04:45.972 --> 00:04:47.722
How many times do I have to say it?

00:05:08.402 --> 00:05:10.856
No, dad was in California
last we heard from him.

00:05:11.424 --> 00:05:14.128
We just thought if he
comes to you for munitions,

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:16.019
Maybe you've seen him
in the last few weeks.

00:05:16.299 --> 00:05:18.046
Just call us if you hear anything. Okay.

00:05:18.195 --> 00:05:19.093
Thanks.

00:05:20.053 --> 00:05:21.151
Caleb hasn't heard from him?

00:05:21.201 --> 00:05:21.874
Nope.

00:05:21.999 --> 00:05:24.244
Neither has Jefferson or pastor Jim.

00:05:24.668 --> 00:05:26.215
What about the journal?
Any leads in there?

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:27.887
No. Same last time I looked.

00:05:27.936 --> 00:05:29.458
Nothing I can make out.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:33.170
I love the guy, but I swear
he writes like freaking Yoda.

00:05:33.171 --> 00:05:34.667
And maybe we should call the feds,

00:05:34.817 --> 00:05:35.865
File a missing person's out.

00:05:35.866 --> 00:05:38.260
We talked about this. Dad would be
pissed if we put the feds on his tail.

00:05:38.261 --> 00:05:39.407
I don't care anymore

00:05:39.532 --> 00:05:41.550
After all that happened back in kansas,

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:42.573
I mean...

00:05:42.823 --> 00:05:43.771
He should have been there, Dean.

00:05:43.772 --> 00:05:45.791
You said so yourself. You
tried to call him and nothing.

00:05:45.866 --> 00:05:46.864
I know.

00:05:47.311 --> 00:05:48.658
I loose my cellphone.

00:05:48.758 --> 00:05:50.604
You know, he could be
dead for all we know.

00:05:50.605 --> 00:05:51.876
Don't say that.

00:05:52.201 --> 00:05:53.723
He's not dead. He's...

00:05:53.822 --> 00:05:56.118
He's what? He's hiding? He's busy?

00:06:02.579 --> 00:06:03.776
I don't believe it.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:05.323
What?

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:11.016
It's a-A text message.

00:06:12.213 --> 00:06:13.336
It's coordinates.

00:06:15.381 --> 00:06:17.253
You think dad was texting us?

00:06:17.449 --> 00:06:18.747
He's given us coordinates before.

00:06:18.797 --> 00:06:20.867
The man can barely work a toaster, Dean.

00:06:21.092 --> 00:06:22.439
Sam, this is good news.

00:06:22.539 --> 00:06:23.936
It means he's okay, or alive.

00:06:24.136 --> 00:06:25.757
Was there a number on the caller I.D.?

00:06:25.807 --> 00:06:27.005
Huh, it said "unknown."

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:28.332
Okay, well, where do
the coordinates point?

00:06:28.382 --> 00:06:29.655
That's the interesting part.

00:06:29.854 --> 00:06:31.301
Rockford, Illinois.

00:06:32.271 --> 00:06:33.469
Okay, and that's interesting how?

00:06:33.519 --> 00:06:36.313
I checked the local rockford
paper. Take a look at this.

00:06:39.678 --> 00:06:41.275
This cop, Walter Kelly,

00:06:41.499 --> 00:06:43.371
Comes home from his
shift, shoots his wife,

00:06:43.495 --> 00:06:45.541
Then puts the gun in his
mouth, blows his brains out.

00:06:45.641 --> 00:06:47.736
Earlier that night,
kelly and his partner

00:06:47.737 --> 00:06:50.294
Responded to a call at
the Roosevelt asylum.

00:06:50.369 --> 00:06:52.888
Okay, I'm not following. What
does this have to do with us?

00:06:52.889 --> 00:06:55.832
Dad earmarked the same
asylum in the journal.

00:06:56.603 --> 00:06:57.851
Let's see.

00:06:59.472 --> 00:07:00.171
Here.

00:07:00.246 --> 00:07:02.890
"Seven unconfirmed
sightings, two deaths"

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:04.487
Till last week, at least.

00:07:04.761 --> 00:07:06.556
I think this is where he wants us to go.

00:07:10.307 --> 00:07:11.429
This is a job.

00:07:13.275 --> 00:07:14.473
Dad wants us to work a job.

00:07:14.548 --> 00:07:16.244
Maybe we'll meet up with
him. Maybe he's there.

00:07:16.245 --> 00:07:17.317
Maybe he's not.

00:07:17.489 --> 00:07:19.560
May He could be sending us there
by ourselves to hunting thing.

00:07:19.561 --> 00:07:20.872
Who cares?

00:07:21.581 --> 00:07:23.477
If he wants us there,
it's good enough for me.

00:07:23.801 --> 00:07:25.523
This doesn't strike you as weird...

00:07:26.521 --> 00:07:27.494
The texting,

00:07:27.741 --> 00:07:29.013
The coordinates? Sam.

00:07:29.388 --> 00:07:31.533
Dad's telling us to go
somewhere. We're going.

00:07:52.517 --> 00:07:54.513
You're Daniel Gunderson,
right, you're cop?

00:07:54.688 --> 00:07:55.461
Yeah.

00:07:56.484 --> 00:07:57.332
I'm...

00:07:57.405 --> 00:07:58.677
Nigel Tufnel

00:07:58.727 --> 00:07:59.849
With the chicago tribune.

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:01.396
Do you mind if I ask a couple questions

00:08:01.397 --> 00:08:02.444
About your partner?

00:08:02.445 --> 00:08:03.392
Yeah, I do.

00:08:03.393 --> 00:08:04.365
I'm just trying to have a beer here.

00:08:04.366 --> 00:08:06.685
I just want to hear
the story in your words.

00:08:07.293 --> 00:08:09.363
A week ago, my partner
was sitting in that chair,

00:08:09.762 --> 00:08:10.910
And now he's dead.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:12.157
Are you gonna ambush me here?

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:12.931
Sorry,

00:08:12.932 --> 00:08:14.527
But I need to know what happened.

00:08:14.652 --> 00:08:17.421
Heyn buddy! How about leaving
the poor guy alone, huh?!

00:08:17.755 --> 00:08:20.200
The man's an officer! Why don't
you show a little respect?!

00:08:27.408 --> 00:08:28.531
You didn't have to do that.

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:29.903
Yeah, of course I did.

00:08:30.635 --> 00:08:31.932
That guy's a serious jerk.

00:08:32.157 --> 00:08:34.028
Let me buy you a beer, huh?

00:08:34.701 --> 00:08:35.699
Two?

00:08:39.317 --> 00:08:40.090
Thanks.

00:08:45.156 --> 00:08:46.603
You shoved me kind of
hard in there, buddy boy.

00:08:46.628 --> 00:08:48.125
I had to sell it, didn't I?

00:08:48.774 --> 00:08:49.971
It's method acting.

00:08:51.019 --> 00:08:51.842
Huh?

00:08:52.339 --> 00:08:53.112
Never mind.

00:08:53.113 --> 00:08:54.235
What did you find out from Gunderson?

00:08:54.335 --> 00:08:56.006
So, Walter Kelly was a good cop.

00:08:56.231 --> 00:08:57.827
Head of his class, even-Keeled.

00:08:57.877 --> 00:08:59.224
He had a bright future ahead of him.

00:08:59.225 --> 00:08:59.873
What about at home?

00:08:59.874 --> 00:09:01.842
He and his wife had a few
fights. Like everybody.

00:09:01.892 --> 00:09:03.364
But it was mostly smooth sailing.

00:09:03.514 --> 00:09:05.110
They were even talking
about having kids.

00:09:05.111 --> 00:09:07.854
All right, so how the kelly had some
deep see the crazy way in the bus

00:09:07.855 --> 00:09:09.227
Or something else did it to him. Right.

00:09:09.324 --> 00:09:11.070
What did Gunderson tell
you about the asylum?

00:09:12.193 --> 00:09:12.891
A lot.

00:09:37.913 --> 00:09:40.632
So, apparently, the cops
chased the kids here...

00:09:42.451 --> 00:09:43.973
Into the south wing.

00:09:46.044 --> 00:09:47.216
South wing, huh?

00:09:47.834 --> 00:09:49.356
Wait a second.

00:09:50.579 --> 00:09:52.475
South wing, south wing.

00:09:55.493 --> 00:09:57.015
"1972,

00:09:57.215 --> 00:09:59.076
Three kids broke into the south wing.

00:09:59.201 --> 00:10:00.673
Only one survived."

00:10:00.872 --> 00:10:02.167
The way he tells it, one of his friends

00:10:02.168 --> 00:10:04.138
Went nuts and started
lighting up the place.

00:10:05.061 --> 00:10:06.707
So, whatever's going on,

00:10:06.882 --> 00:10:08.354
South wing seems like the heart of it.

00:10:08.404 --> 00:10:09.976
Yeah, but if kids are
spelunking the asylum,

00:10:09.977 --> 00:10:11.793
Why aren't there a ton more deaths?

00:10:13.789 --> 00:10:15.710
It looks like the doors
are usually chained.

00:10:16.758 --> 00:10:18.430
They could have been
chained up for years.

00:10:18.923 --> 00:10:20.670
Yeah, to keep people out.

00:10:21.318 --> 00:10:22.965
Or to keep something in.

00:10:33.319 --> 00:10:35.664
Let me know if you see any
dead people, Haley Joel.

00:10:35.814 --> 00:10:36.936
Dude, enough.

00:10:37.834 --> 00:10:39.553
I'm serious. You've got
to be careful. Right.

00:10:39.554 --> 00:10:41.748
Ghosts are attracted to
that E.S.P. Thing you got.

00:10:41.749 --> 00:10:42.946
I told you, it's not E.S.P.

00:10:42.947 --> 00:10:45.166
I just have strange vibes, sometimes,

00:10:45.765 --> 00:10:46.439
Weird dreams.

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:48.352
Yeah, whatever. Don't ask, don't tell.

00:10:48.577 --> 00:10:49.974
Do you get any reading
on that thing or not?

00:10:50.049 --> 00:10:51.970
No. Of course, it doesn't
mean nobody's home.

00:10:52.045 --> 00:10:54.290
Spirits can't appear
during certain hours of day.

00:10:54.315 --> 00:10:55.785
The freaks come out at night.

00:10:56.009 --> 00:10:56.982
Ya. Hey Sam

00:10:57.032 --> 00:10:58.554
Who do you think is a hotter psychic

00:10:58.629 --> 00:11:00.675
Patricia Arquette,
Jennifer Love Hewitt or you?

00:11:27.648 --> 00:11:28.621
Man.

00:11:29.869 --> 00:11:31.216
Electroshock,

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:34.032
Lobotomies. They did some
twisted stuff to these people,

00:11:34.257 --> 00:11:37.175
Kind of like my man
Jack in "cuckoo's nest."

00:11:41.063 --> 00:11:42.884
So, what do you think?

00:11:43.533 --> 00:11:45.154
Ghosts are possessing people?

00:11:45.803 --> 00:11:46.676
Maybe.

00:11:47.524 --> 00:11:50.518
Maybe it's more like Amityville
or the smurl haunting.

00:11:50.714 --> 00:11:53.010
Ah, spirits driving them insane,

00:11:53.633 --> 00:11:55.779
Kind of like my man
Jack in "the shining."

00:11:59.521 --> 00:12:00.491
Dean...

00:12:02.462 --> 00:12:03.585
When are we going to talk about it?

00:12:03.685 --> 00:12:04.333
Talk about what?

00:12:04.358 --> 00:12:05.955
About the fact that dad's not here.

00:12:06.130 --> 00:12:08.076
Oh, uh, let's see, never.

00:12:08.077 --> 00:12:09.024
I'm being serious, man.

00:12:09.025 --> 00:12:09.851
So am I, sam.

00:12:09.852 --> 00:12:12.321
Look. He sent us here. He
obviously wants us here.

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:13.643
We'll just have to pick
up the search later.

00:12:13.644 --> 00:12:15.215
It doesn't matter what he wants.

00:12:15.216 --> 00:12:17.556
See, that attitude right there,

00:12:18.055 --> 00:12:19.577
That is why I always
got the extra cookie.

00:12:19.701 --> 00:12:20.799
Dad could be in trouble.

00:12:20.874 --> 00:12:22.396
We should be looking for him.

00:12:22.421 --> 00:12:25.240
We deserve some answers, Dean. I mean,
this is our family were talking about..

00:12:25.241 --> 00:12:26.659
I understand that, sam,

00:12:26.809 --> 00:12:27.831
But he's given us an order.

00:12:27.832 --> 00:12:29.528
So what ? We've got to
always follow dad's orders?

00:12:29.553 --> 00:12:30.875
Of course we do.

00:12:41.896 --> 00:12:43.643
Sanford Ellicott

00:12:44.865 --> 00:12:45.888
You know what we got to do?

00:12:46.013 --> 00:12:48.103
We've got to find out
more about the south wing,

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:50.177
See if something happened here.

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:07.778
Sam Winchester?

00:13:08.826 --> 00:13:09.575
That's me.

00:13:09.649 --> 00:13:10.647
Come on in.

00:13:16.953 --> 00:13:19.351
Thanks again for see me last minute.

00:13:34.495 --> 00:13:35.593
Dr. Ellicott?

00:13:36.413 --> 00:13:37.611
Ellicott, that name.

00:13:37.885 --> 00:13:40.929
Wasn't there a dr. Sanford Ellicott?

00:13:41.328 --> 00:13:43.947
Yeah, he was a chief
psychiatrist somewhere.

00:13:43.948 --> 00:13:46.989
My father was chief of staff
at the old Roosevelt asylum.

00:13:47.114 --> 00:13:48.162
How did you know?

00:13:48.785 --> 00:13:51.829
Huh, well, I'm sort of
a local-History buff.

00:13:51.976 --> 00:13:55.768
Hey, wasn't there an incident
or something in the...

00:13:55.968 --> 00:13:57.864
In the hospital, I guess,
in the south wing, right?

00:13:57.913 --> 00:13:59.435
We're on your dollar, Sam.

00:14:00.251 --> 00:14:01.873
We're here to talk about you.

00:14:02.796 --> 00:14:04.867
Oh, okay, yeah, yeah, sure.

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:07.733
So? So.

00:14:07.858 --> 00:14:09.005
How's things?

00:14:09.205 --> 00:14:11.550
Uh, things are good, doctor.

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:12.448
Good.

00:14:12.648 --> 00:14:13.895
What you been doing?

00:14:14.741 --> 00:14:15.863
Uh...

00:14:16.487 --> 00:14:18.632
Same old. I've just been on a...

00:14:18.707 --> 00:14:20.728
On a road trip with my brother.

00:14:20.803 --> 00:14:22.025
Was that fun?

00:14:24.094 --> 00:14:25.116
Loads.

00:14:25.665 --> 00:14:26.763
Um...

00:14:27.137 --> 00:14:28.310
You know... We...

00:14:29.507 --> 00:14:30.954
Met a lot of...

00:14:31.703 --> 00:14:32.825
Interesting people.

00:14:32.875 --> 00:14:33.624
Mm-Hmm.

00:14:33.775 --> 00:14:35.297
Did a lot of, uh...

00:14:36.394 --> 00:14:37.991
A lot of interesting things.

00:14:38.814 --> 00:14:39.937
Uh...

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:41.958
You know,

00:14:42.332 --> 00:14:43.430
What was it...

00:14:43.494 --> 00:14:45.415
Exactly that happened in the south wing?

00:14:45.465 --> 00:14:46.413
I forget... Look,

00:14:46.563 --> 00:14:47.960
If you're a local-History buff,

00:14:48.007 --> 00:14:50.003
Then you know all about
the Roosevelt riot.

00:14:50.353 --> 00:14:51.101
The riot?

00:14:51.126 --> 00:14:53.346
Well, no, I know, I'm
just curious -- Sam.

00:14:54.095 --> 00:14:55.517
Let's cut the bull, shall we?

00:14:56.263 --> 00:14:57.760
You're avoiding the subject.

00:15:00.953 --> 00:15:01.852
What subject?

00:15:01.951 --> 00:15:02.800
You.

00:15:03.423 --> 00:15:05.020
Now, I'll make you a deal.

00:15:05.691 --> 00:15:07.886
I'll tell you all
about the Roosevelt riot

00:15:08.061 --> 00:15:10.456
If you tell me something
honest about yourself...

00:15:11.129 --> 00:15:12.152
Like, uh...

00:15:12.748 --> 00:15:14.744
This brother you're road-Tripping with.

00:15:15.243 --> 00:15:16.715
How do you feel about him?

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:28.974
Dude.

00:15:29.074 --> 00:15:31.219
You were in there forever. What
the hell were you talking about?

00:15:31.566 --> 00:15:32.764
Just the hospital, you know.

00:15:32.838 --> 00:15:33.562
And?

00:15:33.637 --> 00:15:35.308
And the south wing,

00:15:35.408 --> 00:15:36.930
It's where they housed
the real hard cases,

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:38.776
Psychotics, the criminally insane.

00:15:38.823 --> 00:15:39.572
Sounds cozy.

00:15:39.597 --> 00:15:41.842
Yeah, and one night in '64, they rioted,

00:15:42.041 --> 00:15:43.962
Attacked the staff, attacked each other.

00:15:44.037 --> 00:15:45.609
So, what, the patients
took over the asylum?

00:15:45.756 --> 00:15:47.278
Apparently. Any deaths?

00:15:47.578 --> 00:15:49.524
Some patients, some staff.

00:15:49.648 --> 00:15:50.796
I guess it was pretty gory.

00:15:50.797 --> 00:15:52.542
Some of the bodies were
never even recovered,

00:15:52.642 --> 00:15:54.663
Including our chief of staff, Ellicott.

00:15:54.664 --> 00:15:55.935
What do you mean "Never recovered"?

00:15:55.963 --> 00:15:57.286
Cops scoured every inch of the place,

00:15:57.336 --> 00:15:59.207
But I guess the patients must have...

00:16:00.354 --> 00:16:02.625
Stuffed the bodies somewhere hidden.

00:16:02.996 --> 00:16:04.094
That's grim. Ya.

00:16:04.568 --> 00:16:06.738
So they transferred all
the surviving patients

00:16:06.739 --> 00:16:08.285
And shut down the hospital for good.

00:16:08.286 --> 00:16:11.275
All right so the * we've got a bunch of
violent deaths and unrecovered bodies.

00:16:11.276 --> 00:16:12.821
Which could mean a
bunch of angry spirits.

00:16:13.096 --> 00:16:15.404
Not good times. Let's check
out the hospital tonight.

00:16:36.127 --> 00:16:37.574
Check this out.

00:16:38.796 --> 00:16:39.769
Creepy...

00:16:41.571 --> 00:16:42.868
Yet terrifying.

00:16:44.739 --> 00:16:46.361
I thought we were going to a movie.

00:16:47.009 --> 00:16:48.881
This is better. It's
like we're in a movie.

00:16:50.774 --> 00:16:52.545
I can't believe you call this a date.

00:16:55.436 --> 00:16:56.858
Come on. That'll be fine.

00:16:57.407 --> 00:16:58.729
That's look around.

00:16:59.328 --> 00:17:00.500
Come on!

00:17:07.461 --> 00:17:08.484
What was that? Ugh!

00:17:12.077 --> 00:17:13.075
Hey, look.

00:17:13.297 --> 00:17:14.719
Come on, let's check it out.

00:17:15.093 --> 00:17:16.540
I don't want to.

00:17:17.314 --> 00:17:18.037
Let's just go.

00:17:18.087 --> 00:17:19.359
Come on.

00:17:22.136 --> 00:17:23.059
Okay.

00:17:23.433 --> 00:17:24.656
Okay. You can wait here.

00:17:24.756 --> 00:17:26.003
Gavin, no.

00:17:26.103 --> 00:17:27.325
I'm just gonna be a minute.

00:17:28.772 --> 00:17:30.693
Nothing's gonna get you, I promise.

00:18:23.496 --> 00:18:24.469
Damn it.

00:18:28.541 --> 00:18:30.761
Hey, sweetie, couldn't take it, huh?

00:18:35.125 --> 00:18:35.998
Hey.

00:18:40.813 --> 00:18:43.033
Gavin, where are you?

00:18:45.411 --> 00:18:46.434
Gavin.

00:19:15.518 --> 00:19:16.641
Getting readings?

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:18.137
No, big-Time.

00:19:18.362 --> 00:19:20.358
This place is orbing like crazy.

00:19:24.347 --> 00:19:26.393
There's probably multiple
spirits out and about.

00:19:26.439 --> 00:19:28.884
And if these unrecovered
bodies are causing the haunting?

00:19:28.885 --> 00:19:30.205
We got to find them and burn them.

00:19:30.255 --> 00:19:30.986
Just be careful.

00:19:30.987 --> 00:19:33.959
The only thing that makes me more
nervous than a pissed-Off spirit

00:19:34.446 --> 00:19:37.217
Is a pissed-Off spirit
of a psycho killer.

00:20:48.166 --> 00:20:48.901
Dean!

00:20:49.636 --> 00:20:50.258
Dean!

00:20:51.050 --> 00:20:51.870
Shotgun!

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:53.341
Sam, get down!

00:21:03.425 --> 00:21:04.415
That was weird.

00:21:04.613 --> 00:21:05.320
Yeah,

00:21:05.715 --> 00:21:06.592
You're telling me.

00:21:08.571 --> 00:21:11.286
No, Dean, I mean, it was weird
that she didn't attack me.

00:21:11.377 --> 00:21:13.186
It looked pretty aggro
from where I was standing.

00:21:13.187 --> 00:21:14.431
She didn't hurt me.

00:21:14.515 --> 00:21:15.703
She didn't even try.

00:21:16.105 --> 00:21:18.452
So she didn't want to hurt
me, then what did she want?

00:21:47.512 --> 00:21:48.983
It's all right.We're
not going to hurt you.

00:21:50.821 --> 00:21:51.895
It's okay.

00:21:52.778 --> 00:21:53.457
What's your name?

00:21:53.485 --> 00:21:54.277
Katherine.

00:21:55.578 --> 00:21:56.454
Kat.

00:21:56.624 --> 00:21:57.359
Okay.

00:21:57.614 --> 00:21:58.660
I'm dean.This is sam.

00:21:58.661 --> 00:21:59.904
What are you doing here?

00:22:01.215 --> 00:22:03.025
My boyfriend, Gavin...

00:22:03.308 --> 00:22:04.354
Is he here?

00:22:04.954 --> 00:22:06.057
Somewhere.

00:22:06.735 --> 00:22:09.676
He thought it would be fun,
try and see some ghosts.

00:22:10.468 --> 00:22:12.193
I thought it was all just...

00:22:13.075 --> 00:22:14.065
You know...

00:22:14.800 --> 00:22:15.931
Pretend.

00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:20.003
I've seen things.

00:22:21.537 --> 00:22:23.431
I heard Gavin scream, and...

00:22:23.516 --> 00:22:25.184
All right, Kat, come on.

00:22:25.524 --> 00:22:27.446
Sam's gonna get you out of here.
Then we're gonna find your boyfriend.

00:22:27.464 --> 00:22:29.076
No, no.

00:22:30.179 --> 00:22:32.130
I'm not gonna leave without Gavin.

00:22:32.385 --> 00:22:33.685
I'm coming with you.

00:22:33.686 --> 00:22:35.728
It's no a joke around
here, okay. It's dangerous.

00:22:35.813 --> 00:22:37.509
That's why I've got to find him.

00:22:39.149 --> 00:22:40.846
All right, I guess we're
gonna split up, then.

00:22:41.096 --> 00:22:42.029
Let's go.

00:22:46.327 --> 00:22:47.401
Gavin!

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:51.990
Gavin!

00:22:55.157 --> 00:22:56.118
Gavin!

00:22:58.720 --> 00:22:59.738
Gavin!

00:23:00.112 --> 00:23:01.497
I've got a question for you.

00:23:01.893 --> 00:23:03.816
You've seen a lot of
horror movies, yeah?

00:23:04.042 --> 00:23:04.834
I guess so.

00:23:04.835 --> 00:23:06.700
Do me a favor. Next time you see one,

00:23:06.870 --> 00:23:07.916
Pay attention.

00:23:08.351 --> 00:23:09.963
When someone says a place is haunted,

00:23:10.246 --> 00:23:11.349
Don't go in.

00:23:26.112 --> 00:23:26.875
Gavin?

00:23:27.497 --> 00:23:28.600
Hey, gavin.

00:23:29.477 --> 00:23:31.626
Hey, it's okay. It's
okay. I'm here to help.

00:23:32.333 --> 00:23:33.039
Who are you?

00:23:33.040 --> 00:23:34.375
My name is Sam.

00:23:34.884 --> 00:23:36.213
We found your girlfriend.

00:23:36.694 --> 00:23:37.571
Kat? Yeah.

00:23:37.572 --> 00:23:38.730
Is she all right?

00:23:38.934 --> 00:23:41.151
She's worried about you. Are you okay?

00:23:42.821 --> 00:23:44.484
I was running. I, uh,

00:23:44.614 --> 00:23:45.690
I think I fell.

00:23:45.691 --> 00:23:47.060
You were running from what?

00:23:48.854 --> 00:23:50.060
There was...

00:23:50.582 --> 00:23:53.328
There was this girl. Her-Her face...

00:23:54.925 --> 00:23:56.067
It was all messed up.

00:23:56.068 --> 00:23:57.110
Okay, listen, listen,

00:23:57.111 --> 00:23:59.099
This girl, did she try to hurt you?

00:23:59.726 --> 00:24:01.780
What? No, she, uh...

00:24:02.595 --> 00:24:03.867
She what?

00:24:05.041 --> 00:24:06.215
She kissed me.

00:24:08.700 --> 00:24:11.537
Um, but she didn't hurt you physically?

00:24:11.732 --> 00:24:13.656
Dude, she kissed me.

00:24:14.308 --> 00:24:15.482
I'm scarred for life.

00:24:16.760 --> 00:24:18.358
Trust me, it could have been worse.

00:24:18.359 --> 00:24:20.021
And now, do you remember anything else?

00:24:20.445 --> 00:24:21.619
She, uh...

00:24:22.467 --> 00:24:24.423
Actually, she tried to
whisper something in my ear.

00:24:25.050 --> 00:24:25.930
What?

00:24:26.745 --> 00:24:28.278
I don't know. I ran like hell.

00:24:42.991 --> 00:24:44.915
You son of a bitch.

00:24:45.697 --> 00:24:47.556
It's all right. I've got a lighter.

00:24:50.674 --> 00:24:52.663
Ow. You're hurting my arm.

00:24:53.674 --> 00:24:54.881
What are you talking about?

00:25:03.681 --> 00:25:06.355
Let me out!Please!

00:25:11.270 --> 00:25:13.433
Kat, hang on!

00:25:41.039 --> 00:25:41.985
What's going on?

00:25:41.986 --> 00:25:43.142
She's inside with one of them.

00:25:43.143 --> 00:25:44.382
Help me!

00:25:44.447 --> 00:25:45.197
Kat!

00:25:45.198 --> 00:25:46.469
Get me out of here!

00:25:46.470 --> 00:25:48.381
Kat, it's not gonna hurt you.

00:25:48.903 --> 00:25:51.544
Listen to me. You have to
face it. You have to calm down.

00:25:51.545 --> 00:25:52.693
She's got to what?

00:25:52.694 --> 00:25:53.606
I have to what?

00:25:53.607 --> 00:25:56.443
These spirits, they don't try to
hurt, they're trying to communicate.

00:25:56.444 --> 00:25:58.041
You've got to listen to.
You've got to face it.

00:25:58.042 --> 00:25:58.986
You face it.

00:25:58.987 --> 00:26:00.617
No. It's the only way you're
gonna get out of there.

00:26:00.618 --> 00:26:01.398
No!

00:26:01.399 --> 00:26:02.572
Look at it.That's all.

00:26:02.637 --> 00:26:03.974
Come on.You can do it.

00:26:25.522 --> 00:26:26.272
Kat?

00:26:28.164 --> 00:26:29.794
Now, I hope you're right about this.

00:26:31.791 --> 00:26:32.998
Yeah, me, too.

00:26:42.924 --> 00:26:44.065
Oh, Kat.

00:26:49.289 --> 00:26:50.659
1, 3, 7.

00:26:51.409 --> 00:26:52.452
Sorry?

00:26:53.789 --> 00:26:55.420
It whispered in my ear

00:26:55.811 --> 00:26:56.952
1, 3, 7.

00:26:57.937 --> 00:26:59.404
Room number.

00:27:02.698 --> 00:27:05.259
All right. So if these spirits
aren't trying to hurt anyone.

00:27:05.260 --> 00:27:06.825
Then what are they trying to do?

00:27:07.151 --> 00:27:08.423
Maybe that's what they've
been trying to tell us.

00:27:08.424 --> 00:27:09.564
I guess we'll find out.

00:27:10.249 --> 00:27:11.194
All right.

00:27:13.842 --> 00:27:14.723
So,

00:27:14.724 --> 00:27:16.940
Now, you guys ready to leave this place?

00:27:17.462 --> 00:27:18.669
That's an understatement.

00:27:18.702 --> 00:27:19.712
Okay.

00:27:20.136 --> 00:27:21.539
You get them out of here.

00:27:21.740 --> 00:27:23.469
I'm gonna gofind room 137.

00:27:32.438 --> 00:27:35.307
So, how do you guys know
about all this ghost stuff?

00:27:36.547 --> 00:27:38.405
It's kind of our job.

00:27:39.455 --> 00:27:41.412
Why would anyone want a job like that?

00:27:43.825 --> 00:27:45.944
I had a crappy guidance counselor.

00:27:48.201 --> 00:27:50.418
And Dean? He's your boss?

00:27:52.733 --> 00:27:53.614
No.

00:28:37.730 --> 00:28:38.740
All right.

00:28:39.001 --> 00:28:40.632
I think we have a small problem.

00:28:41.217 --> 00:28:42.260
Let's break it down.

00:28:42.423 --> 00:28:43.434
I don't think that's gonna work.

00:28:43.564 --> 00:28:44.445
Then a window.

00:28:44.446 --> 00:28:45.097
They're barred.

00:28:45.098 --> 00:28:46.793
How are we supposed to get out?

00:28:48.782 --> 00:28:50.510
That's the point. We're not.

00:28:51.071 --> 00:28:52.376
There's something in here.

00:28:52.506 --> 00:28:53.712
It doesn't want us to leave.

00:28:56.060 --> 00:28:56.941
Those patients.

00:28:57.006 --> 00:28:57.952
No.

00:28:58.473 --> 00:28:59.582
Something else.

00:29:25.340 --> 00:29:27.851
This is why I get paid the big bucks.

00:29:34.400 --> 00:29:35.737
"Patients journal."

00:29:51.934 --> 00:29:54.542
All work and no play makes Dr. Ellicott,

00:29:54.680 --> 00:29:56.669
A very dull boy.

00:30:04.601 --> 00:30:06.390
Right. I've looked everywhere.

00:30:06.672 --> 00:30:07.767
There's no other way out.

00:30:08.143 --> 00:30:09.128
So, what the hell are we gonna do?

00:30:09.191 --> 00:30:10.745
For starters, we're not gonna panic.

00:30:10.885 --> 00:30:11.949
Why the hell not?

00:30:14.484 --> 00:30:15.110
Hey.

00:30:15.157 --> 00:30:16.189
Sam, it's me.

00:30:16.659 --> 00:30:18.364
I see it. It's coming at me.

00:30:18.682 --> 00:30:19.401
Where are you?

00:30:19.402 --> 00:30:20.481
I'm in the basement. Hurry up!

00:30:20.512 --> 00:30:21.420
I'm on my way.

00:30:21.670 --> 00:30:23.751
All right. Can either
of you handle a shotgun?

00:30:24.158 --> 00:30:25.112
What?! No!

00:30:25.566 --> 00:30:26.270
I can.

00:30:27.980 --> 00:30:29.763
My dad took me skeet
shooting a couple times.

00:30:29.810 --> 00:30:30.655
Oh, I heard.

00:30:30.796 --> 00:30:31.828
It's loaded with rock salt.

00:30:31.875 --> 00:30:32.845
Now, it might not kill a spirit,

00:30:32.892 --> 00:30:34.394
But it will repel it,
so if you see something,

00:30:34.551 --> 00:30:35.051
Shoot.

00:30:35.067 --> 00:30:35.724
Okay.

00:30:35.959 --> 00:30:36.569
Okay.

00:30:43.286 --> 00:30:44.083
Dean!

00:31:02.655 --> 00:31:03.515
Dean!

00:32:04.622 --> 00:32:05.452
Dean?

00:32:33.013 --> 00:32:34.296
Don't be afraid.

00:32:34.640 --> 00:32:36.142
I'm going to make you all better.

00:32:43.447 --> 00:32:44.495
Hey, Gavin.

00:32:46.237 --> 00:32:46.941
Yeah?

00:32:48.677 --> 00:32:50.398
If we make it out of here alive,

00:32:51.587 --> 00:32:53.105
We are so breaking up.

00:32:56.544 --> 00:32:57.592
Did you hear that?

00:32:57.764 --> 00:32:58.828
Something's coming.

00:33:02.489 --> 00:33:03.882
Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!

00:33:04.492 --> 00:33:05.822
Don't shoot! It's me!

00:33:06.072 --> 00:33:07.735
Sorry. Sorry.

00:33:08.314 --> 00:33:09.581
Son of a...

00:33:13.915 --> 00:33:15.167
What are you still doing here?

00:33:15.438 --> 00:33:16.392
Where's Sam?

00:33:16.705 --> 00:33:18.144
He went to the basement. You called him.

00:33:18.989 --> 00:33:19.787
I didn't call him.

00:33:19.917 --> 00:33:21.043
His cellphone rang.

00:33:21.340 --> 00:33:22.295
He said it was you.

00:33:24.329 --> 00:33:25.314
Basement, huh?

00:33:29.630 --> 00:33:30.474
All right.

00:33:31.585 --> 00:33:32.571
Watch yourselves.

00:33:34.761 --> 00:33:35.856
And watch out for me.

00:33:42.080 --> 00:33:42.878
Sammy?

00:33:44.615 --> 00:33:45.866
Sam, you down here?

00:33:46.758 --> 00:33:47.572
Sam!

00:33:50.075 --> 00:33:50.971
Sam!

00:33:53.303 --> 00:33:54.038
Man...

00:33:54.820 --> 00:33:56.432
Answer me when I'm calling you.

00:33:56.995 --> 00:33:57.574
You all right?

00:33:57.575 --> 00:33:58.638
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:33:58.779 --> 00:34:00.202
You know that wasn't
me who called, right?

00:34:00.300 --> 00:34:02.286
Yeah, I know. I think
something lured me down here.

00:34:02.287 --> 00:34:03.648
I think I know who

00:34:03.867 --> 00:34:04.727
Dr. Ellicott.

00:34:05.169 --> 00:34:07.375
That's what the spirits have been trying
to tell us. You haven't seen him, have you?

00:34:07.469 --> 00:34:08.283
No.

00:34:08.471 --> 00:34:09.425
How do you knowit was him?

00:34:09.426 --> 00:34:10.770
Because I found his logbook.

00:34:10.802 --> 00:34:13.336
Apparently, he was
experimenting on his patients.

00:34:13.826 --> 00:34:14.952
Awful stuff.

00:34:14.983 --> 00:34:16.658
Makes lobotomies look
like a couple of aspirin.

00:34:16.659 --> 00:34:18.300
But it was the patients who rioted.

00:34:18.301 --> 00:34:20.053
Yeah. They were rioting
against Dr. Ellicott.

00:34:21.304 --> 00:34:24.782
Dr. Feelgood was working on some
sort of extreme-Rage therapy.

00:34:24.783 --> 00:34:27.113
He thought if he could get his
patients to vent their anger,

00:34:27.223 --> 00:34:28.506
Then they'd be cured of it.

00:34:28.897 --> 00:34:30.196
Instead it only made
them worse and worse

00:34:30.197 --> 00:34:31.447
And angrier and angrier.

00:34:31.651 --> 00:34:33.090
I'm thinking, what if his spirit

00:34:33.309 --> 00:34:34.529
Is doing the same thing?

00:34:34.764 --> 00:34:35.531
To the cop,

00:34:35.645 --> 00:34:37.022
The kids in the '70s

00:34:37.335 --> 00:34:39.697
Making them so angry
they become homicidal.

00:34:40.777 --> 00:34:41.449
Come on.

00:34:41.731 --> 00:34:43.421
We've got to find his
bones and torch them.

00:34:43.921 --> 00:34:44.766
How?

00:34:45.086 --> 00:34:46.400
The police never found his body.

00:34:46.462 --> 00:34:49.185
The logbook said he had some
hidden procedure room down here

00:34:49.186 --> 00:34:51.328
Somewhere where he'd
work on his patients. So,

00:34:51.474 --> 00:34:53.273
If I was a patient, I'd
drag his ass down here

00:34:53.274 --> 00:34:54.634
Do a little work on myself.

00:34:54.681 --> 00:34:56.089
I don't know.It sounds kind of...

00:34:56.152 --> 00:34:56.871
Of crazy?

00:34:56.872 --> 00:34:57.387
Yeah.

00:34:57.388 --> 00:34:58.858
Yeah, exactly.

00:35:14.858 --> 00:35:16.110
I told you I looked everywhere.

00:35:16.111 --> 00:35:17.815
I didn't find a hidden room.

00:35:18.191 --> 00:35:19.771
Well, that's why they call it hidden.

00:35:22.701 --> 00:35:23.765
You hear that?

00:35:25.204 --> 00:35:26.112
What?

00:35:36.978 --> 00:35:38.229
There's a door here.

00:35:41.609 --> 00:35:42.532
Dean.

00:35:47.938 --> 00:35:49.518
Step back from the door.

00:35:54.472 --> 00:35:55.818
Sam, put the gun down.

00:35:56.193 --> 00:35:57.351
Is that an order?

00:35:59.025 --> 00:36:00.699
That's more of a friendly request.

00:36:00.700 --> 00:36:02.999
'Cause I'm getting pretty
tired of taking your orders.

00:36:04.631 --> 00:36:05.726
I knew it.

00:36:06.321 --> 00:36:07.479
Ellicott did something
to you, didn't he?

00:36:07.480 --> 00:36:08.699
For once in your life,

00:36:09.122 --> 00:36:10.029
Shut your mouth.

00:36:10.030 --> 00:36:11.427
What are you gonna do, sam?

00:36:11.953 --> 00:36:13.696
The gun's filled with rock salt.

00:36:13.888 --> 00:36:14.920
It's not gonna kill me.

00:36:18.284 --> 00:36:18.910
No.

00:36:19.207 --> 00:36:20.115
But it'll hurt like hell.

00:36:28.108 --> 00:36:28.906
Sam.

00:36:29.531 --> 00:36:31.112
We've got to burn Ellicott's bones,

00:36:31.143 --> 00:36:32.520
And all this will be over,

00:36:32.885 --> 00:36:34.105
And you'll be back to normal.

00:36:34.277 --> 00:36:35.325
I am normal.

00:36:36.358 --> 00:36:37.969
I'm just telling the
truth for the first time.

00:36:38.470 --> 00:36:40.191
I mean, why are we even here?

00:36:40.989 --> 00:36:43.685
'Cause you're following dad's
orders like a good little soldier?

00:36:43.779 --> 00:36:46.297
'Cause you always do what
he says without question?

00:36:46.595 --> 00:36:48.597
Are you that desperate for his approval?

00:36:48.801 --> 00:36:50.240
This isn't you talking, Sam.

00:36:50.308 --> 00:36:51.904
That's the difference
between you and me.

00:36:52.123 --> 00:36:54.000
I have a mind of my own.

00:36:54.250 --> 00:36:56.018
I'm not pathetic like you.

00:36:56.019 --> 00:36:58.099
So what are you gonna do?
Huh. You gonna kill me?

00:36:58.146 --> 00:37:01.072
We're no closer to finding dad today

00:36:58.146 --> 00:37:01.072
You know, I am sick of
doing what you tell me to do.

00:37:01.562 --> 00:37:03.456
We're no closer to finding dad today

00:37:03.564 --> 00:37:05.395
Than we were six months ago.

00:37:07.277 --> 00:37:08.560
Well, then here.

00:37:08.810 --> 00:37:10.641
Let me make it easier for you.

00:37:12.831 --> 00:37:13.801
Come on.

00:37:13.989 --> 00:37:14.943
Take it.

00:37:15.297 --> 00:37:18.144
Real bullets are gonna work a hell
of a lot better than rock salt.

00:37:19.208 --> 00:37:20.100
Take it.

00:37:31.981 --> 00:37:33.483
You hate me that much?

00:37:35.110 --> 00:37:36.941
You think you can kill your own brother?

00:37:39.819 --> 00:37:41.164
Then go ahead.

00:37:42.385 --> 00:37:43.652
Pull the trigger.

00:37:50.011 --> 00:37:51.231
Do it!

00:38:08.773 --> 00:38:11.120
Man, I'm not gonna give
you a loaded pistol.

00:38:18.597 --> 00:38:19.833
Sorry, Sammy.

00:39:23.269 --> 00:39:24.739
Oh, that's just gross.

00:39:33.804 --> 00:39:34.884
Soak it up.

00:39:47.761 --> 00:39:49.170
Don't be afraid.

00:39:50.003 --> 00:39:51.396
I'm going to help you.

00:39:51.505 --> 00:39:53.336
I'm going to make you all better.

00:40:44.524 --> 00:40:46.386
You're not gonna try
and kill me, are you?

00:40:49.296 --> 00:40:50.125
No.

00:40:50.959 --> 00:40:51.815
Good.

00:40:53.196 --> 00:40:55.152
'Cause that would be awkward.

00:41:01.350 --> 00:41:02.492
Thanks, guys.

00:41:02.821 --> 00:41:04.010
Yeah, thanks.

00:41:04.401 --> 00:41:06.466
No more haunted asylums, okay?

00:41:13.894 --> 00:41:14.864
Hey, Dean.

00:41:16.256 --> 00:41:17.837
I' sorry, man. I

00:41:19.088 --> 00:41:20.950
said some awful thingsback there.

00:41:21.518 --> 00:41:22.785
You remember all that?

00:41:23.176 --> 00:41:24.037
Yeah.

00:41:25.727 --> 00:41:28.605
It's like I couldn't control
it, but I didn't mean it

00:41:29.012 --> 00:41:29.982
Any of it.

00:41:30.671 --> 00:41:31.625
You didn't, huh?

00:41:32.647 --> 00:41:33.664
No. Of course, not.

00:41:36.532 --> 00:41:38.112
Do we need to talk about this?

00:41:39.129 --> 00:41:40.005
No.

00:41:40.091 --> 00:41:42.868
I'm not really in the sharing
and caring kind of mood.

00:41:43.474 --> 00:41:45.023
I just want to get some sleep.

00:42:00.337 --> 00:42:01.197
Dean.

00:42:08.835 --> 00:42:09.695
Hello.

00:42:12.699 --> 00:42:13.419
Dad?



00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.000
